; RoundEndHeap14 -- the map change on a texture heap too small for two
; maps (null card capped at 14 MB; Hamiller's Radeon has 16, which a long
; game fills as far): ZOD_ROUNDEND 12, orig01 and orig02 in turn, the next
; map unpaused, GL only, music off. Before the fix (21.11.) every change to
; orig02 logged "no room for the 1152x1440 map ... the map stays undrawn"
; and the map stayed undrawn for the round (the user's trails on
; Hamiller). Must hold now: no "stays undrawn", "drawn black for want of a
; texture 0", "earlier maps' textures deleted" > 0.
; LIMIT 600
FailAt 1000
Wait 5
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/zod-#?
Echo "0" >DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
Echo "Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map" >>DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
Echo "Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig02.map" >>DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
SetEnv ZOD_ROUNDEND 12
SetEnv RadeonGLHeapMax 14
Echo "=== GL (null card, 14 MB heap), many map changes ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZod rh1 120 -u -l DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-rh1.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-rh1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/zod-rh1-lib.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
UnSetEnv RadeonGLHeapMax
UnSetEnv ZOD_ROUNDEND
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
